Vendored third-party libraries
==============================

These libraries are bundled so that Abinova's built-in document
importers and spell/grammar checking build without requiring users
to install external dependencies.  Each is compiled as a libtool
convenience library (noinst, PIC) and linked statically into
`libabinova` — the plugins they once belonged to were moved into the
core tree (`src/wp/impexp/`, `src/wp/ap/grammar/`).

  librevenge-0.0.6   document-format support library (LGPL-2.1+/MPL-2.0)
                     shared base used by libwpd, libwpg, libwps
  libwpd-0.10.3      WordPerfect document import (LGPL-2.1+/MPL-2.0)
                     used by the built-in .wpd importer
  libwps-0.4.14      MS Works document import (LGPL-2.1+/MPL-2.0)
                     used by the built-in .wps importer
  libwpg-0.3.4       WordPerfect Graphics import (LGPL-2.1+/MPL-2.0)
                     used by the built-in .wpg image importer
  wv-1.2.9           legacy .doc (OLE2/Word 97) import (GPL-2.0+)
                     vendored with local security patches so no
                     system libwv is required
  hunspell-1.7.0     spell-checking engine (MPL-1.1/GPL-2.0/LGPL-2.1)
                     used by the built-in spell and Hunspell-based
                     grammar checking (HUNSPELL_STATIC, no shared
                     library installed)

Only the library source subsets are vendored (inc/ + src/lib/ plus
licenses); upstream tools, fuzzers, tests and build scripts are not
included. The convenience-lib Makefile.am in this directory replaces
the upstream build systems.

To update a vendored library: drop in the new upstream tree, keep the
same directory layout (inc/, src/lib/ — or src/hunspell/ for
hunspell), refresh the _SOURCES list in Makefile.am, and check the
license header list above is still accurate.
